### Output Format

```json
{
  "segments": [
    {"start": 0, "end": 120, "duration": 120},
    {"start": 300, "end": 305, "duration": 5}
  ],
  "total_segments": 2,
  "total_duration_seconds": 125
}
```

Note: adjacent/overlapping segments are merged. For example, inputs `{"start":522,"end":524}` and `{"start":525,"end":527}` (gap of 1s, within default `--merge-gap 2`) are combined into a single `{"start":522,"end":527,"duration":5}` segment in the output.
